ef rid="T1FN3" ref-type="table-fn">c</xref>, % (95% CI)</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Male</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">64.6 (55.4-72.8)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">48.2 (43.2-53.2)</td><td align="right" rowspan="2" valign="middle" colspan="1">&#x0003c;.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Female</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">35.4 (27.2-44.6)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">51.8 (46.8-56.8)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="col" colspan="4" rowspan="1"><bold>Education<xref rid="T1FN3" ref-type="table-fn">c</xref>, % (95% CI)</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Less than high school education</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">30.7 (21.9-41.2)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">25.5 (21.8-29.7)</td><td align="right" rowspan="3" valign="middle" colspan="1">.10</td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">High school or GED</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">32.1 (23.7-41.8)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">23.7 (19.1-29.0)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Some college or greater</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">37.2 (28.0-47.6)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">50.8 (45.2-56.3)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="col" colspan="4" rowspan="1"><bold>Health insurance, % (95% CI)</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Present</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">93.4 (88.8-96.2)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">88.5 (84.9-91.3)</td><td align="right" rowspan="2" valign="middle" colspan="1">.40</td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Absent</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6.6 (3.8-11.2)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">11.5 (8.7-15.1)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" s